# RevScope backend configuration.
#
# Copy this file to .env in the directory you run revscope from (revscope/ in
# development) and fill in the values. Real environment variables take
# precedence over the file. Never commit your .env.
#
# Only DATABASE_URL and INTEGRATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY are required. Everything
# else is optional: uncomment a line to set it. An uncommented but empty value
# isn't always the same as leaving it unset, so keep unused options commented.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres connection URL for the main (accounts) database. Migrations run
# automatically on startup. Example: postgres://user:password@localhost/revscope
DATABASE_URL=

# Encrypts integration credentials (Stripe keys, etc.) stored in the database.
# 64 hex characters (32 bytes). Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Keep it safe: credentials encrypted with a lost key can't be recovered.
INTEGRATION_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Server -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Address for plain HTTP. Default: 127.0.0.1:4320. Use 0.0.0.0:80 to serve
# publicly, or keep a loopback address behind a reverse proxy.
# REVSCOPE_LISTEN=

# Set to true when Cloudflare proxies all traffic: plain HTTP is then only
# answered for Cloudflare and loopback peers (and Let's Encrypt challenges), so
# the origin can't be reached directly. HTTPS is unaffected. Default: off.
# REVSCOPE_REQUIRE_CLOUDFLARE=

# Set to true behind a reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy, Traefik, ...) that
# appends the visitor's address to X-Forwarded-For. The last value of that
# header is then used as the visitor IP for geolocation and visitor counts.
# Only enable it when the proxy is the only way to reach the server, or
# visitors can forge their IP. Not needed behind Cloudflare. Default: off.
# REVSCOPE_TRUST_X_FORWARDED_FOR=

# Most client connections held open at once, idle keep-alives included.
# Connections over the cap are closed as soon as they're accepted. The cap is
# lowered at startup if the open file limit (ulimit -n, LimitNOFILE) can't fit
# it with room to spare, so raise that limit too. Default: 100000.
# REVSCOPE_MAX_CONNECTIONS=

# Address for HTTPS, e.g. 0.0.0.0:443. Setting it enables HTTPS with automatic
# Let's Encrypt certificates. Leave unset when a proxy terminates TLS.
# REVSCOPE_LISTEN_TLS=

# Comma-separated hostnames to get certificates for when REVSCOPE_LISTEN_TLS is
# set, e.g. analytics.example.com. The first is served to clients that send no
# hostname, and is the CNAME target for projects' custom domains.
# Default: eu1.revscope.co,api.revscope.co (the hosted service). Required in a
# self-hosted build, which refuses to start without it.
# REVSCOPE_TLS_DOMAINS=

# Comma-separated contacts (emails) for the Let's Encrypt account, used for
# certificate expiry notices.
# REVSCOPE_ACME_CONTACT=

# Set to true to use Let's Encrypt's staging environment (untrusted
# certificates, looser rate limits) while testing a deployment. Staging keeps
# its account and certificates in a staging/ subdirectory of the ACME dir.
# REVSCOPE_ACME_STAGING=

# Where ACME account credentials and certificates are stored. Default: data/acme
# REVSCOPE_ACME_DIR=

# Public URL of the web app, used in emailed links (password reset, invites).
# Default: https://www.revscope.co. For a self-hosted
# build with the bundled UI: https://analytics.example.com/ui
# APP_BASE_URL is read as a fallback when this is unset.
# REVSCOPE_WEB_BASE_URL=

# Public URL of the API, used in MCP OAuth metadata. Defaults to the Host the
# request arrived on; set it when that differs from the public origin, e.g.
# behind a proxy. Example: https://api.example.com
# REVSCOPE_API_BASE_URL=

# Comma-separated hostnames allowed to call the API cross-origin with the
# session cookie, i.e. where a separately deployed web app is served.
# `*.example.com` matches subdomains only. Loopback is always allowed.
# Default: revscope.co,*.revscope.co (empty for self-hosted builds). Set it
# empty when the UI is only served by this process.
# REVSCOPE_CORS_ORIGINS=

# Log level filter, e.g. info, error, or revscope=debug. Default: warn.
# RUST_LOG=

# Set to true to disable the demo project's overview cache (for development).
# REVSCOPE_DISABLE_OVERVIEW_CACHE=

# --- Sign in with Google and Apple ---------------------------------------------

# Each one shows a button on the login and signup forms when set. The server
# checks the ID tokens the browser gets against the provider's public keys, so
# no client secret is needed.
#
# The client id of a "Web application" OAuth client in Google Cloud. Add the
# web UI's origin (e.g. https://analytics.example.com) to its authorized
# JavaScript origins.
# REVSCOPE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
#
# The Services ID of Sign in with Apple in the Apple Developer account. Register
# the web UI's domain, and its origin followed by `/` as a return URL.
# REVSCOPE_APPLE_CLIENT_ID=

# --- Connect with Google (Google Analytics imports) ----------------------------

# With both this secret and REVSCOPE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID set, Google Analytics
# imports offer "Connect with Google"; without them, only a service account key
# works. Add REVSCOPE_WEB_BASE_URL followed by /oauth/google-analytics to the
# OAuth client's authorized redirect URIs.
# REVSCOPE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Email (password reset, invites) ------------------------------------------

# MailChannels API key. Without it, no email is sent; self-hosted invite links
# are still shown in Settings for you to send yourself.
# MAILCHANNELS_API_KEY=

# Sender address, e.g. noreply@example.com. Required to send email.
# MAILCHANNELS_FROM_EMAIL=

# Sender display name. Default: RevScope
# MAILCHANNELS_FROM_NAME=

# MailChannels send endpoint. Default: https://api.mailchannels.net/tx/v1/send
# MAILCHANNELS_API_URL=

# --- AI chat tab --------------------------------------------------------------
# The Ask tab is enabled when both REVSCOPE_CHAT_URL and REVSCOPE_CHAT_API_KEY
# are set, and hidden otherwise.

# Base URL of an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, without /chat/completions, such as
# a Cloudflare AI Gateway's
# https://gateway.ai.cloudflare.com/v1/<account_id>/<gateway>/compat
# REVSCOPE_CHAT_URL=

# Model provider API key, sent as the bearer token.
# REVSCOPE_CHAT_API_KEY=

# Token for an authenticated Cloudflare AI Gateway, sent as its
# cf-aig-authorization header. Leave unset if yours isn't authenticated.
# REVSCOPE_CHAT_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# Model to use, as provider/model. Default: grok/grok-4.7
# REVSCOPE_CHAT_MODEL=

# --- Error reporting ----------------------------------------------------------

# Sentry DSN. Errors are reported to Sentry when set.
# SENTRY_DSN=
